IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgb1-s156-interests`
IMPORT `sgb2-s162-loans-to-directors`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- the procedure for a director's declaration of interest (s 156) and for a loan or other restricted transaction in favour of a director (s 162),
-- as a regulative layer over the Boolean encodings in sgb1-s156-interests.l4 and sgb2-s162-loans-to-directors.l4.
--
-- What is here: s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer declares the interest at a meeting or sends a written notice, and what follows each route
-- (s 156(9) the company's copy, s 156(10) the notice deemed part of the next meeting, s 156(11) the minutes); s 156(6) to (8) the conflicting office or property,
-- with the first meeting of s 156(7); s 156(15) the offence.
-- s 162(2) the company's bar on a restricted transaction; s 162(3) and (4) the exception for expenditure or a home, with the prior approval of (4)(a) (and s 162(10)),
-- or the condition of (4)(b) and its six months; s 162(5) the indemnity; s 162(6) the offence; s 162(7) recovery.
-- The parties are the corpus's own `Party` (sg-core.l4). The gates are the existing section functions, called and not restated.
-- A MUST with no WITHIN carries no LEST (the unstable build warns that such a LEST can never be reached), so the duties with no day below have no breach path of their own; s 156(15) and s 162(2), (4)(b) and (6) are where a breach arises.
-- Each DEONTIC is gated: where the gate does not answer JUST TRUE, nothing is owed and the rule is FULFILLED at once.
-- Left to the Boolean encodings and not restated: the definitions (s 156(3), (4), (5), (13); s 162(1), (8), (9)), the persons of s 156(9) (named in the act below), and the rest of s 162(3) (paragraphs (c) and (d)) and ss 163A and 163B, taken as one fact.
-- Not encoded: s 156(12) (the directors must permit a chief executive officer who is not a director to attend a meeting: no day, no step after it, and sgb1-s156-interests.l4 already has the DEONTIC);
-- the second limb of s 156(11) (the records of "written resolution duly signed and returned": the section nowhere else speaks of a written resolution); s 156(14).

DECLARE `s 156 declaration act` IS ONE OF
    `s 156(1)(a) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors of the company`
    `s 156(1)(b) send a written notice to the company on the nature, character and extent of the interest`
    `s 156(9) send a copy of the written notice to all the directors, or all the other directors where a director gave it`
    `s 156(11) record the declaration in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made`
    `s 156(10)(b) record the declaration in the minutes of the next meeting of the directors after the notice is given, as if it had been made at that meeting`
    `s 156(6)(a) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors of the company`
    `s 156(6)(b) send a written notice to the company on the conflict`
    `s 156(15) fail to comply with a provision of section 156`

DECLARE `s 162 loan act` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction`
    `s 162(4)(b) repay the amount of the restricted transaction or discharge the liability under it`
    `s 162(5) indemnify the company against the loss arising from the restricted transaction`
    `s 162(6) authorise the making of the restricted transaction`
    `s 162(7) recover the amount of the loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement, or the amount for which the company becomes liable`

§ `Section 156(1), (9), (10) and (11): the declaration, the copy and the minutes`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the relevant facts come to the director's or chief executive officer's knowledge; counting="as soon as is practicable after the relevant facts have come to his or her knowledge" (not a number of days, so no clock is encoded; for the written notice the same words run from the dates in subsection (2), and for the copy and the minutes the text sets no day at all)
-- FORK: s 156(1) | the two routes (a) a declaration at a meeting and (b) a written notice are alternatives (ROR), each open at once and with no clock, because "as soon as is practicable" is not a number | a MUST with a deadline set from a number of days the text does not give
-- FORK: s 156(1) | the declarant is any `Party` the caller passes, a Director, or an Officer for a chief executive officer who is not a director, because sg-core.l4 has no constructor for a chief executive officer | a new constructor in sg-core.l4
-- FORK: s 156(10) | the deeming of the written notice into the next meeting is encoded as a step the secretary owes after the notice (the minutes of that meeting, s 156(10)(b) with (11)), for the deeming itself is not a duty | the deeming left as a Boolean with no step
-- FORK: s 156(9) and (10) | the company's copy and the secretary's minute after a written notice are two duties owed together (RAND), neither depending on the other | the minute as the step after the copy
-- FORK: s 156(11) | the secretary's duty to minute a declaration has no day in the text, so it is a MUST with no clock and no breach path | a duty to minute at or before the next meeting
-- src:12938 | 156.—(1) Subject to this section, every director or chief executive
-- src:12939 | officer of a company who is in any way, whether directly or indirectly,
-- src:12940 | interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company
-- src:12941 | must as soon as is practicable after the relevant facts have come to his
-- src:12942 | or her knowledge —
-- src:12944 | (a) declare the nature of his or her interest at a meeting of the
-- src:12945 | directors of the company; or
-- src:12947 | (b) send a written notice to the company containing details on
-- src:12948 | the nature, character and extent of his or her interest in the
-- src:12949 | transaction or proposed transaction with the company.
@ref s 156(1) Disclosure of interests in transactions, property, offices, etc. (src:12938-12949)
