GIVEN declarant IS A Party
      company IS A Party
      secretary IS A Party
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in any way, whether directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not deemed to be interested by reason of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 declaration act`
`s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` MEANS
    IF `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the nature of the interest or send a written notice` `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` `the person is in any way, whether directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company` `the person is not deemed to be interested by reason of subsection (4)` `the interest consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction` `the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN ((PARTY declarant
           MUST `s 156(1)(a) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors of the company`
           HENCE (PARTY secretary
                  MUST `s 156(11) record the declaration in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made`
                  HENCE FULFILLED))
          ROR
          (PARTY declarant
           MUST `s 156(1)(b) send a written notice to the company on the nature, character and extent of the interest`
           HENCE ((PARTY company
                   MUST `s 156(9) send a copy of the written notice to all the directors, or all the other directors where a director gave it`
                   HENCE FULFILLED)
                  RAND
                  (PARTY secretary
                   MUST `s 156(10)(b) record the declaration in the minutes of the next meeting of the directors after the notice is given, as if it had been made at that meeting`
                   HENCE FULFILLED))))
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 156(6) to (8): the conflict of duty or interest`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property if already a director or chief executive officer, otherwise the day the person became one (s 156(7)(a), (b), s 156(8)); counting="at the first meeting of the directors of the company held" after that day for a declaration under (6)(a), the first meeting being day n, the days from day 0 to the date of that meeting, computed from the DATE inputs by DATE_SERIAL; "as soon as is practicable after" that day for a written notice under (6)(b) (no number, so no clock)
-- FORK: s 156(7) | a first meeting that passes without a declaration under (6)(a) is not by itself a breach: the declaration route has lapsed and the written notice of (6)(b), which has no day, is still owed | a breach at the first meeting, the written notice having no part (as in sgb1-s156-interests.l4)
-- FORK: s 156(7) | where no meeting has yet been held after the day, there is no first meeting and no clock: the duty is open with no day | a clock from the date of the next meeting once it is called
-- src:13046 | (6) Every director and chief executive officer of a company who
-- src:13047 | holds any office or possess any property whereby, whether directly or
-- src:13048 | indirectly, any duty or interest might be created in conflict with their
-- src:13049 | duties or interests as director or chief executive officer (as the case
-- src:13050 | may be) must —
-- src:13052 | (a) declare at a meeting of the directors of the company the
-- src:13053 | fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict; or
-- src:13055 | (b) send a written notice to the company setting out the fact
-- src:13056 | and the nature, character and extent of the conflict.
-- src:13058 | [36/2014]
@ref s 156(6) Disclosure of interests in transactions, property, offices, etc. (src:13046-13058)
