GIVEN declarant IS A Party
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds any office or possesses any property whereby any duty or interest might be created in conflict with the person's duties or interests as director or chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE
      `the date the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A DATE
      `the dates of the meetings of the directors` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 declaration act`
`s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` MEANS
    IF `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict or send a written notice` `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` `the person holds any office or possesses any property whereby any duty or interest might be created in conflict with the person's duties or interests as director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (CONSIDER `s 156(7) the meeting of the directors at which the declaration under subsection (6)(a) must be made` `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer` `the date the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` `the dates of the meetings of the directors`
          WHEN JUST firstMeeting THEN
              ((PARTY declarant
                MUST `s 156(6)(a) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors of the company`
                WITHIN ((DATE_SERIAL firstMeeting) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL (`s 156(8) the date after which the written notice under subsection (6)(b) must be given as soon as practicable` `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer` `the date the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property`)))
                HENCE FULFILLED
                LEST (PARTY declarant
                      MUST `s 156(6)(b) send a written notice to the company on the conflict`
                      HENCE FULFILLED))
               ROR
               (PARTY declarant
                MUST `s 156(6)(b) send a written notice to the company on the conflict`
                HENCE FULFILLED))
          WHEN NOTHING THEN
              ((PARTY declarant
                MUST `s 156(6)(a) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors of the company`
                HENCE FULFILLED)
               ROR
               (PARTY declarant
                MUST `s 156(6)(b) send a written notice to the company on the conflict`
                HENCE FULFILLED)))
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 156(15): the offence`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the person fails to comply with a provision of section 156; counting=silent (the text puts no day on the offence, and "as soon as is practicable" gives the duties above no day on which a failure is certain, so the failure is an event the trace supplies)
-- FORK: s 156(15) | the offence is a separate DEONTIC whose forbidden act is the failure itself, a finding made outside the trace, because the duties above carry no clock to lapse on; the penalty ("a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months", "or" and not "or both") is in the BECAUSE text | the offence as the LEST step of each duty above
-- src:13163 | (15) Any director or chief executive officer of a company who fails
-- src:13164 | to comply with any of the provisions of this section shall be guilty of
-- src:13165 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:13166 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months.
-- src:13168 | [36/2014]
@ref s 156(15) Disclosure of interests in transactions, property, offices, etc. (src:13163-13168)
GIVEN declarant IS A Party
      `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 declaration act`
`s 156(15) a director or chief executive officer must not fail to comply with a provision of section 156` MEANS
    IF `s 156(15) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY declarant
         SHANT `s 156(15) fail to comply with a provision of section 156`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY declarant BECAUSE "the director or chief executive officer failed to comply with a provision of section 156 and is guilty of an offence, liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 162(3), (4) and (10): the exception and the approval it needs`

-- The helpers below are Boolean and are asserted in the tests; the DEONTICs that follow call them.
