-- src:13509 | (a) with the prior approval of the company given at a general
-- src:13510 | meeting at which the purposes of the expenditure and the
-- src:13511 | amount or extent of the restricted transaction are disclosed;
-- src:13512 | or
-- src:13514 | (b) on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is
-- src:13515 | not given as aforesaid at or before the next following
-- src:13516 | annual general meeting, the amount of or liability under the
-- src:13517 | restricted transaction must be repaid or discharged (as the
-- src:13518 | case may be) within 6 months from the conclusion of that
-- src:13519 | meeting.
@ref s 162(4)(b) Loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements (src:13506-13519)
GIVEN `the date the transaction was made` IS A DATE
      `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 162(4)(b) the days from the day of the transaction to the last day for repayment or discharge` MEANS
    (DATE_SERIAL (`s 162(4)(b) the last day on which the amount or liability must be repaid or discharged` `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes`)) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the date the transaction was made`)

§ `Section 162(2): the company must not make a restricted transaction`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company makes the restricted transaction; counting=silent (the bar has no time limit; the day of the transaction decides only whether an approval came before it, from the DATE inputs)
-- FORK: s 162(2) | where the transaction is made on the condition of (4)(b), the making is not a breach: the exception of (3) is met when the condition is, and what follows is owed under (4)(b) | the making a breach until the repayment is in
-- FORK: s 162(2) | the one `Party` the bar binds is the company named; the exception and the exemption are facts the caller supplies | none
-- src:13457 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4) and sections 163A and 163B,
-- src:13458 | a company (other than an exempt private company) must not make a
-- src:13459 | restricted transaction.
@ref s 162(2) Loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements (src:13457-13459)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      `the company is an exempt private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is within section 163A or 163B or section 162(3)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred for the purposes of the company or to enable the director to perform his or her duties, section 162(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is for a home of a director in full-time employment, section 162(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another such transaction for a home is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company approved the transaction at a general meeting disclosing the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company gave its approval` IS A DATE
      `the date the transaction was made` IS A DATE
      `the transaction was made on the condition in section 162(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 162 loan act`
`s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` MEANS
    IF `the company is an exempt private company` OR `the transaction is within section 163A or 163B or section 162(3)(c) or (d)`
       OR `s 162(3) and (4) the transaction is within paragraph (a) or (b) and subsection (4) authorises it` `the transaction is to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred for the purposes of the company or to enable the director to perform his or her duties, section 162(3)(a)` `the transaction is for a home of a director in full-time employment, section 162(3)(b)` `another such transaction for a home is outstanding` `the company approved the transaction at a general meeting disclosing the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent` `the date the company gave its approval` `the date the transaction was made` `the transaction was made on the condition in section 162(4)(b)`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY company
         SHANT `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY company BECAUSE "a company that is not an exempt private company made a restricted transaction outside every exception, and contravened section 162"

§ `Section 162(4)(b): repayment within six months from the next annual general meeting`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company makes the restricted transaction; counting="within 6 months from the conclusion of that meeting", the meeting being the next following annual general meeting: the last day is that meeting's conclusion plus 6 months (sg-periods P1, P4, the existing function s 162(4)(b)), and n is the days from day 0 to that last day, computed from the two DATE inputs by DATE_SERIAL
-- FORK: s 162(4)(b) | the bearer of "must be repaid or discharged" is the relevant director, the one who owes the amount (the text is passive), and a failure is charged to the company as its contravention of section 162 | no bearer, or the company as the bearer
-- FORK: s 162(4)(b) | the six months run unless the company gave the approval (4)(a) describes before the transaction was made, which also meets the condition of (4)(b) | the six months run in every case
-- src:13506 | (4) Subsection (3)(a) or (b) does not authorise the making of any
-- src:13507 | restricted transaction, except —
-- src:13509 | (a) with the prior approval of the company given at a general
-- src:13510 | meeting at which the purposes of the expenditure and the
-- src:13511 | amount or extent of the restricted transaction are disclosed;
-- src:13512 | or
-- src:13514 | (b) on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is
-- src:13515 | not given as aforesaid at or before the next following
-- src:13516 | annual general meeting, the amount of or liability under the
-- src:13517 | restricted transaction must be repaid or discharged (as the
-- src:13518 | case may be) within 6 months from the conclusion of that
-- src:13519 | meeting.
@ref s 162(4)(b) Loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements (src:13506-13519)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      director IS A Party
      `the transaction is to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred for the purposes of the company or to enable the director to perform his or her duties, section 162(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is for a home of a director in full-time employment, section 162(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another such transaction for a home is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company approved the transaction at a general meeting disclosing the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company gave its approval` IS A DATE
      `the date the transaction was made` IS A DATE
      `the transaction was made on the condition in section 162(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 162 loan act`
`s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF (`s 162(3)(a) or (b) the transaction is within one of the two paragraphs` `the transaction is to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred for the purposes of the company or to enable the director to perform his or her duties, section 162(3)(a)` `the transaction is for a home of a director in full-time employment, section 162(3)(b)` `another such transaction for a home is outstanding`)
       AND `the transaction was made on the condition in section 162(4)(b)`
       AND (NOT (`s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` `the company approved the transaction at a general meeting disclosing the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent` `the date the company gave its approval` `the date the transaction was made` `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes`))
    THEN PARTY director
         MUST `s 162(4)(b) repay the amount of the restricted transaction or discharge the liability under it`
         WITHIN (`s 162(4)(b) the days from the day of the transaction to the last day for repayment or discharge` `the date the transaction was made` `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY company BECAUSE "the amount was not repaid or the liability not discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting, so the condition of section 162(4)(b) failed and the company contravened section 162"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 162(5): the indemnity of the directors who authorised the transaction`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the conclusion of the next following annual general meeting without the prior approval; counting=silent ("jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss arising therefrom" has no day, so no clock is encoded)
-- FORK: s 162(5) | one DEONTIC for one authorising director; "jointly and severally" is not a thing a single party's duty can say, so the caller runs the rule once for each director who authorised | one rule with a list of directors
-- FORK: s 162(5) | the indemnity is owed once the next following annual general meeting has passed without an approval given before the transaction, even before the six months are out | owed only when the six months have run out and the amount is unpaid (the text says "loss", which a late repayment may leave nil)
-- src:13526 | (5) Where the prior approval of the company is not given as
-- src:13527 | required by the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b), the
-- src:13528 | directors authorising the making of the restricted transaction are
-- src:13529 | jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss
-- src:13530 | arising therefrom.
@ref s 162(5) Loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements (src:13526-13530)
GIVEN director IS A Party
      `the transaction is to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred for the purposes of the company or to enable the director to perform his or her duties, section 162(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is for a home of a director in full-time employment, section 162(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another such transaction for a home is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company approved the transaction at a general meeting disclosing the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company gave its approval` IS A DATE
      `the date the transaction was made` IS A DATE
      `the transaction was made on the condition in section 162(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 162 loan act`
`s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction must indemnify the company against the loss` MEANS
    IF (`s 162(3)(a) or (b) the transaction is within one of the two paragraphs` `the transaction is to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred for the purposes of the company or to enable the director to perform his or her duties, section 162(3)(a)` `the transaction is for a home of a director in full-time employment, section 162(3)(b)` `another such transaction for a home is outstanding`)
       AND (`s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss` `the transaction was made on the condition in section 162(4)(b)` (`s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` `the company approved the transaction at a general meeting disclosing the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent` `the date the company gave its approval` `the date the transaction was made` `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY director
         MUST `s 162(5) indemnify the company against the loss arising from the restricted transaction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 162(6): the offence of the authorising director`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company makes the restricted transaction; counting=silent (no time limit)
-- FORK: s 162(6) | the offence is a separate DEONTIC: where the company contravenes section 162, the director SHANT authorise the making, and authorising it is the breach; the penalty ("a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years", "or" and not "or both") is in the BECAUSE text | the offence as the next step of the company's rule above
-- src:13534 | (6) Where a company contravenes this section, any director who
-- src:13535 | authorises the making of the restricted transaction shall be guilty of an
-- src:13536 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:13537 | $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years.
@ref s 162(6) Loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements (src:13534-13537)
GIVEN director IS A Party
      `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 162 loan act`
`s 162(6) where the company contravenes section 162 a director must not authorise the making of the restricted transaction` MEANS
    IF `s 162(6) the director is guilty of the offence` `the company contravened section 162` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY director
         SHANT `s 162(6) authorise the making of the restricted transaction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY director BECAUSE "the director authorised the making of a restricted transaction that contravened section 162 and is guilty of an offence, liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 162(7): recovery of the amount`

-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company makes the dealing contrary to section 162; counting=silent (the text gives no day for the recovery, and only says nothing in the section prevents it)
-- FORK: s 162(7) | "Nothing in this section operates to prevent the company from recovering" is a liberty of the company, a MAY with no clock and nothing owed if it is never used | no step, the subsection being only a saving
-- src:13541 | (7) Nothing in this section operates to prevent the company from
-- src:13542 | recovering the amount of any loan, quasi‑loan, credit transaction or
-- src:13543 | arrangement or amount for which it becomes liable under any
-- src:13544 | guarantee entered into or in respect of any security given contrary to
-- src:13545 | this section.
@ref s 162(7) Loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements (src:13541-13545)
GIVEN company IS A Party
      `the amount is owed under a dealing made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 162 loan act`
`s 162(7) the company may recover the amount of a dealing made contrary to section 162` MEANS
    IF `s 162(7) section 162 operates to prevent the company from recovering the amount` `the amount is owed under a dealing made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY company
         MAY `s 162(7) recover the amount of the loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement, or the amount for which the company becomes liable`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
